flow "Circuit breaker"
summary "How a circuit breaker stops hammering a failing service, then probes for recovery."
tags resilience fault-tolerance microservices
level beginner
source "https://martinfowler.com/bliki/CircuitBreaker.html"
related distributed-systems/retry-backoff-dlq

node client "Client" actor
node breaker "Circuit Breaker: CLOSED" state state=success
node payments "Payments API" service
edge client > breaker
edge breaker > payments

scenario trip "Failures trip the breaker"
  step healthy "Closed: calls flow"
    "While **closed**, every call passes straight through to Payments and the breaker just counts failures."
    send client > breaker "charge"
    send breaker > payments "charge"
    state payments success
  step failing "Payments starts failing"
    "Payments begins timing out. The breaker records each failure; the threshold is 3 in a row."
    detail "Simple breakers trip on a consecutive failure count that resets on success. Production breakers often track error rate (such as a 50% failure rate) or set separate thresholds per failure class (for example, 10 timeouts versus 3 connection failures) while ignoring normal domain errors."
    state payments error
    send client > breaker "charge"
    send breaker > payments "charge"
    label breaker "Breaker: CLOSED (3 fails)" with
    state breaker warning
  step open "Open: fail fast"
    "Threshold reached, so the breaker **opens**. New calls are rejected instantly and Payments gets room to recover."
    detail "Failing fast keeps callers from tying up resources waiting on timeouts and stops extra traffic from hitting an already struggling supplier. Callers still need a fallback strategy—returning an error, queuing work like a payment authorization for later, or serving acceptable stale data."
    label breaker "Breaker: OPEN"
    state breaker error
    send client > breaker "charge"
    send breaker > client "503 fast-fail"
    callout breaker "No call reaches Payments" with

scenario recover "Half-open probe succeeds" from=trip/open
  step half-open "Half-open: one probe"
    "After the cool-down the breaker goes **half-open** and lets a single probe call through."
    label breaker "Breaker: HALF-OPEN"
    state breaker pending
    state payments success
    send breaker > payments "probe"
  step closed-again "Closed again"
    "The probe succeeded, so the breaker **closes** and normal traffic resumes. A failed probe would have re-opened it."
    label breaker "Breaker: CLOSED"
    state breaker success
    send client > breaker "charge"
    send breaker > payments "charge"
